# Dark Mode Parity

All new and edited UI must work correctly in **both** light and dark mode.

## What must work in dark mode

- Nutrition Facts panels, the content below them, and barcodes
  (e.g. `pages/add-product.html`).
- Popovers and their text (including the locked-input hover popover).
- Chat inputs, streaming, and chart/streaming accent colors.

## Rules for the agent

- Theme is **global**, controlled via the `wise-theme` / `chat-theme`
  localStorage keys and the `dark` class on `<html>`. Do not add per-page theme
  toggles, and do not force a page to load dark first.
- Before considering any visual change done, verify it in dark mode as well as
  light (use the `visual-verify` skill to capture both).
- When adding colors, define the dark-mode counterpart at the same time — never
  ship a light-only value.
